{"authored" [{"question" "q-161712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nThe triple integral above is defined over the type III region given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2x,\\,0\\le y\\le xz}.\n$$\n\nFor a fixed admissible $x$, let $[a(x),b(x)]$ be the full nonempty $z$ fiber of the exactly specified region $S$. What is $a(x)+b(x)$?" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161712/review.json" "file_sha256" "8621356198ecc4d195137a159d2660fc2592034101e2bcde166c45c2e836235c" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161712/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "df14600841eeb2faad830f9046c2d8b203053c8c6a0d8b72b09897143f4f9972" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161712/verification.json" "basis" 2082 "rationale" "Preserve S and key2x; actual x projection[0,2] excludes negative x where z bounds reverse."} {"question" "q-161712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The defining set $S$ is retained exactly. The requirement $0\\le z\\le2x$ has no solution for $x<0$, so the actual outer range is $0\\le x\\le2$. For each such $x$, the full $z$ interval is $[0,2x]$, and $xz\\ge0$ makes the $y$ interval $[0,xz]$ nonempty. Hence\n\n$$a(x)+b(x)=0+2x=2x,\\qquad \\iiint_S f\\,dV=\\int_0^2\\int_0^{2x}\\int_0^{xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.$$\n\nFor $f=1$, the true volume is $\\int_0^2 2x^3\\,dx=8$. The source solution retained the nominal outer range $[-1,2]$ and included reversed $z$ bounds on negative $x$, giving the signed value $15/2$. That outer-bound error does not change the requested middle-endpoint sum $2x$." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161712/review.json" "file_sha256" "8621356198ecc4d195137a159d2660fc2592034101e2bcde166c45c2e836235c" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161712/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "df14600841eeb2faad830f9046c2d8b203053c8c6a0d8b72b09897143f4f9972" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161712/verification.json" "basis" 2082 "rationale" "Preserve S and key2x; actual x projection[0,2] excludes negative x where z bounds reverse."} {"question" "q-161712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161712/review.json" "file_sha256" "8621356198ecc4d195137a159d2660fc2592034101e2bcde166c45c2e836235c" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161712/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "df14600841eeb2faad830f9046c2d8b203053c8c6a0d8b72b09897143f4f9972" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161712/verification.json" "basis" 2082 "rationale" "Preserve S and key2x; actual x projection[0,2] excludes negative x where z bounds reverse."} {"question" "q-161712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nThe triple integral above is defined over the type III region given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2x,\\,0\\le y\\le xz}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/state.json" "file_sha256" "788a9691568f64cb7c13aa285ad76c93e87db7b16a06c4ae123e8caa4136a543" "basis" 2077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A type III region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {u}_{2}(x,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/assets/0603bed12c6af74e46544d8bebc52362aed95a9a5ad7418ea4faaf228f3b5241.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type III region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(x,z)=0,\\,{u}_{2}(x,z)=xz.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}[{\\int }_{0}^{xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dz\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}{\\int }_{0}^{xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=(0)+(2x)=2x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/state.json" "file_sha256" "788a9691568f64cb7c13aa285ad76c93e87db7b16a06c4ae123e8caa4136a543" "basis" 2077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "27b5b7a888138e758a90a755e287632e41cbd828d2ec0cea0caf31069fdb088a" "basis" 2077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/state.json" "file_sha256" "788a9691568f64cb7c13aa285ad76c93e87db7b16a06c4ae123e8caa4136a543" "basis" 2077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/state.json" "file_sha256" "788a9691568f64cb7c13aa285ad76c93e87db7b16a06c4ae123e8caa4136a543" "basis" 2077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/state.json" "file_sha256" "788a9691568f64cb7c13aa285ad76c93e87db7b16a06c4ae123e8caa4136a543" "basis" 2077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariabl